      "comment": "The judge's own rationale finds no unsupported claim. The reply uses only what the researcher stated: died 1861 in Pulaski County, born about 1823, parents James and Elizabeth. It doesn't move the parents to the county the research was already working, which was the original failure in issue #3266. The reasoning is sound genealogy: a man who died in 1861 can't marry in 1870, so h_002's identification fails."
